        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric of silk damask and metal thread, Iran, 1800-1899"@en , "Dress fabric of silk damask and metal thread.\n\nWoven silk and metal thread damask, twill binding.\nWarp: dark blue silk, Z-twist.\nWeft: silk: dark blue, green, light red, all indeterminable twist and white silk, S-twist.\nMetal thread: silver-gilt strip open s-wound on yellow silk and open S-wound on white silk, both indeterminable twist.\nDark blue ground with small dark blue pattern of flowers and stems. The main pattern is one complete and two partial large 7-petalled flowers with small boteh shaped leaves all outlined in light red and worked in either 'gold' or 'silver'."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e1f23dd2-7955-3b7c-a271-563e55f920fb> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of silk damask and metal thread.\n\nWoven silk and metal thread damask, twill binding.\nWarp: dark blue silk, Z-twist.\nWeft: silk: dark blue, green, light red, all indeterminable twist and white silk, S-twist.\nMetal thread: silver-gilt strip open s-wound on yellow silk and open S-wound on white silk, both indeterminable twist.\nDark blue ground with small dark blue pattern of flowers and stems. The main pattern is one complete and two partial large 7-petalled flowers with small boteh shaped leaves all outlined in light red and worked in either 'gold' or 'silver'."@en , "Dress fabric of silk damask and metal thread, Iran, 1800-1899"@en ;
